  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "When people price a degree, they count the tuition. But the biggest cost is invisible, the years you weren't earning.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "lock",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "coin"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "Tuition isn't",
            "the real cost."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Economists call it opportunity cost, the salary you gave up to sit in class instead.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "lock",
          "kicker": "the hidden cost",
          "line": "Opportunity cost",
          "sub": "the income you skipped"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Education economics weighs that lost income against future gains.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-edecon",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · education economics"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Four years out of the workforce can mean a hundred thousand dollars or more in forgone pay.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "lock",
          "big": "$100K+",
          "label": "in wages you skipped",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "x"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "And that's on top of the tuition you actually paid.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-tuition",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · tuition"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Add compounding, and investing those lost wages could have grown into a small fortune.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "lock",
          "big": "$1M+",
          "label": "had you earned & invested",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "chartUp"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Which is before counting the interest on the loans themselves.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-loans",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · student loans"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A degree can still win, but only if it earns back tuition and those lost years.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Must beat both",
          "props": [
            "coin",
            "clock"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The smartest question isn't what does it cost, but what does it cost you to wait.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "flash",
          "bg": "ink",
          "line": "Cost of waiting",
          "props": [
            "clock",
            "coin"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s9"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The payoff depends entirely on what, and where, you study.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-ushe",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · US higher education"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s10"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So when you chose, did you actually count the lost years?",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "question",
